    "content": "Altruism\n\nVoluntary actions that help another person with a work problem. Instructing a new hire on how to use equipment, helping a coworker catch up with a backlog of work, fetching materials that a colleague needs and cannot procure on their own. Interpersonal helping\n\nFocuses on helping coworkers in their jobs when such help was needed. Courtesy\n\nHelping Behavior (Taking on the forms of altruism, interpersonal helping, courtesy, peacemaking, and cheerleading.)\n\nSubsumes all of those foresightful gestures that help someone else prevent a problem. Touching base with people before committing to actions that will affect them, providing advance notice to someone who needs to know to schedule work. Peacemaking\n\nActions that help to prevent, resolve, or mitigate unconstructive interpersonal conflict. Cheerleading",
