    "topic_path": "Personality, Attitudes, and Work Behaviors/Work Attitudes/What Causes Positive Work Attitudes?",
    "content": "As we have seen earlier in this chapter, personality and values play important roles in how employees feel about their jobs.\n\nAnother source of stress has to do with the roles people are expected to fulfill on and off the job. Role ambiguity is uncertainty about what our responsibilities are in the job. Role conflict involves contradictory demands at work; it can also involve conflict between fulfilling one’s role as an employee and other roles in life, such as the role of parent, friend, or community volunteer.",
